{"id": "sevt_01V689CdUntpeM5ccfL7Uori", "content": [{"text": "The 500s come from commit `a3f9c21`, a checkout deploy that replaced one batched query with a query per order. That change exhausted the DB connection pool.\n\n- **Deploy timing:** `a3f9c21` (\"refactor order summary builder for readability\") deployed to checkout at 14:31:18. Checkout p99 jumped from about 75 ms to about 3,850 ms at 14:31 and kept climbing to about 5 s.\n- **Error timing:** `error_rate` stayed at 0 until 14:40, then ran at roughly 0.1\u20130.67 through 14:59. It started about 9 minutes after the latency jump, which fits the pool filling up under load.\n- **Other deploys:** cart, auth and inventory deployed at 09:14, 11:02 and 14:55. The first two were well before the spike. Inventory came 24 minutes after latency jumped and 15 minutes after errors began, so it can't have started either.\n- **Diff:** `build_summary` used to fetch all order items in one `order_id IN (...)` query and group them in memory. It now runs `OrderItem.objects.filter(order_id=...)` once per open order. That is the per-row query where there used to be a batch.\n- **Log:** the log has 3,320 per-order `SELECT * FROM order_items WHERE order_id = ?` lines. The errors are `DB connection pool exhausted (active=50/50, waiters=12)`, followed by `request_end status=500 ... error=PoolTimeout`. They hit `/api/checkout/summary` and also `/api/checkout/validate`, which fits a shared pool running dry.\n\nFix: roll back `a3f9c21`, or restore the batched `order_id__in` query with in-memory grouping. The 500s come from pool exhaustion, so they should clear once the query count drops. I haven't checked `db_pool_utilization` on the other services, so I can't say whether they were affected. Confidence is high.\n\n**Root cause:** `a3f9c21` \u2014 the checkout summary refactor replaced one batched `order_items` query with one query per order, which exhausted the 50-connection DB pool and made requests fail with `PoolTimeout` 500s.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-14T11:44:58.904376Z", "type": "agent.message"}
